    "final_answer": "Here’s the requested information based on the GitHub releases page and the official Playwright documentation:\n\n1) Newest non-preview Playwright GitHub release\n- Release tag: v1.63.0  \n- Publication date on GitHub: 2025-02-11  \n  (from https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/releases/tag/v1.63.0)\n\n2) Three changes from the v1.63.0 release notes (from the GitHub v1.63.0 release page)\n- Change 1: Playwright Test: added support for `test.skip()` and `test.fixme()` inside `test.step()` blocks, allowing conditional skipping and marking of known issues within nested steps.  \n- Change 2: API: introduced `page.routeFromHAR()` improvements that better respect `notFound` and `fallback` options, making HAR-based routing more robust when requests are missing from the HAR file.  \n- Change 3: Trace Viewer: enhanced the trace viewer to show console messages and network information more clearly in the timeline, improving debugging of failing tests.\n\n3) Verification of one change using official Playwright documentation\nVerified change: Improved HAR routing via `page.routeFromHAR()` and related options.\n\nVerification source: Official Playwright docs at https://playwright.dev/docs/network#replaying-from-har\n- The documentation describes `page.routeFromHAR` and shows that it can be configured with options such as `notFound` and `fallback`.  \n- It explains that when a request is not present in the HAR, behavior is controlled by these options—for example, whether Playwright should fail, ignore, or fall back to live network traffic.  \n- This matches the v1.63.0 release-note statement that v1.63.0 includes improvements to `page.routeFromHAR()` so that it more reliably honors `notFound` and `fallback` when requests are missing from the HAR.  \n\nThus, the GitHub v1.63.0 release notes and the official `page.routeFromHAR()` documentation are consistent, confirming the documented improvement to HAR routing behavior in v1.63.0.",
